corpora.said:
gate 1b's C lexer reads a preprocessing directive where the pinned GCC does not (a /*/ opener does not close its own block comment, 'int a;
/*/
#define FOO
*/
#ifdef FOO
int b;
#endif
int z;
'): its directive readers keep ('a', 'b', 'z') and the pinned GCC 14.3 at -std=gnu99 keeps ('a', 'z'), so an arm one of them grades is an arm the other compiles, or drops
